# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the values. `.env*` is ignored by
# git on purpose, so the real file never lands in a commit — this one is the
# template that shows up in the repo.
#
# Vercel: Project → Settings → Environment Variables, same names, no NEXT_PUBLIC
# prefix removal (they must keep it, the browser needs them).

# --- Supabase: Project Settings → API -------------------------------------
# The account pages and cloud sync read these two. With both present the forms
# in src/components/AuthPanel.tsx can be wired to supabase.auth.*; until then the
# pages say that the cloud is not connected yet.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# --- OAuth -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase owns both providers: enable Google and GitHub under Authentication →
# Providers, paste the client id and secret there, then set the redirect URL to
# <your-site>/auth/callback. Nothing else belongs in this file — the browser only
# ever sees the anon key above.
#
# Google: https://console.cloud.google.com → APIs & Services → Credentials →
#   OAuth client ID (Web application) → authorised JS origins = your site,
#   authorised redirect URIs = https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback
# GitHub: https://github.com/settings/developers → OAuth Apps → New OAuth App →
#   Homepage = your site, Authorization callback URL =
#   https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback
